      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A new class of chiral atropoisomeric (P, N) ligand precursors has been obtained with excellent diastereoselectivities and high yields through diastereoselective metal-free intramolecular radical oxidative C-H amination with chiral phosphamide as the auxiliary group. This method provides a concise and highly valuable pathway for the synthesis of enantiopure aminophosphine ligands in large-scale."},
